    "title": "Crimson Desert Is Out Soon: Here’s What Comes in Each Edition - IGN",
    "text": "Crimson Desert is an open-world action-adventure game that’s set to release on PS5, Xbox, and PC on Thursday, March 19. Developed by Pearl Abyss, the company behind Black Desert Online, it looks seriously ambitious in all the best ways. It’s available for preorder now (see it at Amazon) in two editions and includes a preorder bonus, the contents of which are detailed below. Let’s take a look.Crimson Desert Standard EditionCrimson Desert Deluxe Edition (Physical)PS5Get it at Amazon - $89.99Get it at Best Buy - $89.99Get it at GameStop - $89.99Get it at Walmart - $89.99XboxGet it at Amazon - $89.99Get it at Best Buy - $89.99Get it at GameStop - $89.99Get it at Walmart - $89.99Physical copies of the deluxe edition of Crimson Desert are nearly entirely sold out at the time of the writing (only the Xbox version is available at Amazon). If you can get your hands on it, however, it comes with the game, the preorder bonus, as well as the following items:Physical ItemsDeluxe Edition BoxDeluxe Edition Limited Edition SteelbookLetter from the DeveloperGreymane Brooch Pin3 Character Photo Cards3 PatchesMap of PywelDigital ItemsKairos Plate Set: Kairos Plate Helm, Kairos Plate Gloves, Kairos Plate Boots, Kairos Cloak, Kairos Plate ArmorBalgran ShieldExclaire Horse Set: Exclaire Champron, Exclaire Barding, Exclaire Saddle, Exclaire StirrupsCrimson Desert Deluxe Edition (Digital)Digital Copy - $79.99PS5: PS StoreXbox: Xbox StorePC: Fanatical ($67.99) | GMG ($67.99) | Steam | EpicThe digital deluxe edition of the game costs $10 less than the physical version, but it lacks the physical goodies. Fanatical and GMG have the Steam PC version on sale as well. Here are the digital items it includes:Kairos Plate Set: Kairos Plate Helm, Kairos Plate Gloves, Kairos Plate Boots, Kairos Cloak, Kairos Plate ArmorBalgran ShieldExclaire Horse Set: Exclaire Champron, Exclaire Barding, Exclaire Saddle, Exclaire StirrupsCrimson Desert Preorder BonusPreorder the game on any platform and in any edition, and you’ll receive the following digital item:Khaled ShieldPreorder the PS5 version, and you’ll get the following digital items:Grotevant Plate Set: Grotevan Plate Helm, Grotevan Plate Armor, along with Grotevan cloak, gloves, and bootsCrimson Desert Global Release TimesWant to know when you'll be able to play? Here's the list. For more info, check out the Crimson Desert release times.Los Angeles: 3pm, March 19Dallas: 5pm, March 19New York: 6pm, March 19Sao Paulo: 7pm, March 19London: 10pm, March 19Berlin: 11pm, March 19Paris: 11pm, March 19Cape Town: Midnight, March 19Istanbul: 1am, March 20Dubai: 2am, March 20Singapore: 6am, March 20Beijing: 6am, March 20Seoul: 7am, March 20Tokyo: 7am, March 20Sydney: 9am, March 20What Is Crimson Desert?Crimson Desert is a medieval fantasy-themed game set in the land of Pywel, where you play as Kliff, captain of the Greymanes, as the ruthless Black Bear army executes a brutal attack that leaves the Greymane forces scattered. Your job is to explore the world to reunite with your comrades and rebuild what’s been lost. As you do so, you’ll forge new alliances and discover even more dangerous threats looming over the land.The journey takes you through all sorts of environments, from plains to deserts to mountains. You can ride mounts ranging from horses to wolves and dragons. You even have a Zelda-style glider that lets you leap from mountain peaks and soar over the land.Although there’s some debate on social media about whether Crimson Desert is an RPG, developer Pearl Abyss doesn’t label it as such. It calls Crimson Desert “an open-world action-adventure game.” That’s because it doesn’t have character leveling or experience points. You do expand your capabilities, but you do so by finding items in the open world, like in an action-adventure game like Zelda or a Metroid.Based on the trailers, it does look like a hodgepodge of popular game elements. It has an extensive combat system, an explorable open world, puzzles, giant monsters to fight, and more. Here’s hoping the game is not too good to be true.Other Preorder Guides007 First Light Preorder Guide The Adventures of Elliot: The Millennium Tales Preorder Guide Castlevania: Belmont's Curse Preorder Guide Disney Afternoon Collection (Switch) Preorder Guide Final Fantasy VII Rebirth (Switch 2) Preorder Guide Forza Horizon 6 Preorder Guide Indiana Jone and the Great Circle (Switch 2) Preorder Guide LEGO Batman: Legacy of the Dark Knight Preorder Guide Marvel Tōkon: Fighting Souls Preorder Guide Metal Gear Solid: Master Collection Vol. 2 Pragmata Preorder Guide Saros Preorder Guide Silent Hill: Townfall Preorder Guide Starfield (PS5) Preorder Guide Tomodachi Life: Living the Dream Preorder Guide Yoshi and the Mysterious Book Preorder Guide Chris Reed is a commerce editor and deals expert for IGN. He also runs IGN's board game and LEGO coverage. You can follow him on Bluesky.",
